Profiling tools for finding where a program's CPU and wakeups go on NetBSD
(docs/app-syscalls-2026-10-31.org).  Copied to /var/tmp on the Nano.

lwptime PID [SECS]   exact CPU per thread over SECS, from kinfo_lwp l_rtime
                     (measured at every context switch).  Use this, not DTrace
                     profile-997: on NetBSD that provider fires on the 100 Hz
                     clock and over-samples threads woken in step with it (the
                     cubeb audio thread read 5.3 % there, 0.55 % here).
sysprof.sh PID [SECS] syscall rates by call, by thread (with LWP names), and
                     by thread x call, from ktrace.
fftree.sh PID [SECS] lwptime for a process, all its descendants (Firefox's
                     fork server makes content processes grandchildren) and
                     Mahogany.
ffsym.sh PROF PMAP NAMES  aggregate DTrace "tid pc kernel count" samples by
                     library, thread and libxul symbol (unstripped libxul from
                     the pkgsrc work dir, base from pmap).

cc -O2 -o lwptime lwptime.c
